---
const providers = [
  { name: "OpenAI", sub: "direct API key", mark: "01" },
  { name: "Anthropic", sub: "direct API key", mark: "02" },
  { name: "Google Gemini", sub: "Google AI API key", mark: "03" },
  { name: "GitHub Copilot", sub: "eligible GitHub account", mark: "04" },
  { name: "OpenRouter", sub: "models available to your account", mark: "05" },
  { name: "Mistral AI", sub: "direct API key", mark: "06" },
  { name: "Local or custom", sub: "OpenAI-compatible endpoint", mark: "07" },
];
---

<section id="providers" class="container">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="section-num">04 — Providers</span>
    <h2>Connect the provider that fits the task.</h2>
    <p>Use a direct API, an eligible account integration, a CLI-backed session, or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Model usage and provider subscriptions remain separate from Limitcode Pro.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="providers-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="provider-list">
        {providers.map((p) => (
          <div class="provider">
            <span class="mark">{p.mark}</span>
            <span class="name">{p.name}</span>
            <span class="sub">{p.sub}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Your provider relationship stays yours.</h3>
      <p>Provider usage, subscriptions, rate limits, and model availability remain with the provider or endpoint you connect. Change provider or model from the active chat session.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 14px;">OpenAI-compatible endpoints such as Ollama, LM Studio, LiteLLM, or a custom gateway can keep inference local.</p>

      <div class="note">
        <span class="kicker">Data flow</span>
        Prompts and any context or tool results included in a request go to the provider or endpoint you selected. Credentials are stored in your Sublime Text settings. Activation uses the Limitcode service.
      </div>

      <a class="docs-link" href="/providers">Compare every connection method →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
